    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI converted owner deletion into a soft-delete across the Spring Boot stack:\n\n**Domain model** \u2014 `Owner.java`\n- Added a `deleted` boolean field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\", nullable = false)`) defaulting to `false`, with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`. A newly created owner is therefore `deleted = false`.\n\n**API contract** \u2014 `openapi.yml`\n- Added a `deleted` boolean property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps `owner.deleted \u2192 dto.deleted`. `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns the flag.\n\n**Controller** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`\n- `deleteOwner` no longer removes the row; it sets `deleted = true` and saves, returning `204 NO_CONTENT` (2xx). The record is retained, and `GET` still returns it with `deleted: true`.\n- The create endpoint's checks now ignore soft-deleted owners: filtered `existing.isDeleted()` out of `isDuplicate` (the identity-key gate), `findHousemates` (the household duplicate block), and `findPossibleDuplicateOf` (the possible-duplicate flag). So a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match is deleted.\n\n**Persistence schema/seed** \u2014 added a `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) and appended the value to the positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)` seed rows (hsqldb \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 and mysql; h2/postgres use named-column inserts that pick up the default).\n\nBoth new acceptance tests pass: `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` (delete flags `deleted` true and retains the record) and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` (recreating a soft-deleted owner is allowed).\n\nOne note: the pre-existing MySQL seed data was already positionally inconsistent with the MySQL schema (8 insert values vs. many columns); I kept my change internally consistent by adding the matching value, but MySQL isn't exercised by the test suite (which runs on hsqldb).",
